  ('writing-just-for-fun', 311, 'Splash out a poem made of colors you can hear, like a loud red or a whispering green.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 312, 'Walk slowly down one store aisle or past a bakery case and describe its colors.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 313, 'Weave a short fable with a gentle lesson, starring a snail who refuses to hurry.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 314, 'Spin a list at a summer picnic of everything the ants might be saying about your lunch.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 315, 'Number ten small things you could write about someday, then pick the silliest and write a paragraph.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 316, 'Let your umbrella speak in a short poem where it boasts about every storm it has weathered.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 317, 'Rest your hands in your lap and describe them in four honest, gentle sentences.'),
