  ('writing-just-for-fun', 340, 'Read aloud a poem you wrote before, just to hear your own words in the room.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 341, 'Choose a word you''ve never liked and write a kind little poem that gives it a second chance.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 342, 'Introduce the oldest thing you own to someone who has never seen it, its marks, smell and weight.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 343, 'Collect two characters from different stories you love and write a scene where they meet in a waiting room.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 344, 'Take turns with a friend writing reviews of imaginary restaurants on the moon.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 345, 'Keep a pencil tucked behind your ear while you garden in spring, ready for any idea that grows.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 346, 'Wait for the toast to pop and write a little poem with a pop at the end of every line.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 347, 'Stand at your kitchen sink and describe the view in front of you, even if it is only a wall and a sponge.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 348, 'Sneak a tiny bit of magic into an ordinary office scene, like a stapler that only works when someone says please.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 349, 'Let a kid choose a title, any title at all, and write the story that goes with it together.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 350, 'Enjoy writing for five minutes after dinner with the dishes still waiting, just because you want to.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 351, 'Rearrange the letters of a short word into new words, then string them into one odd sentence.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 352, 'Open a window on the first warm spring day and describe the air that drifts in.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 353, 'Answer the question "What did the snow see last night?" in a short story of five sentences.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 354, 'Leave a riddle on a sticky note on the bathroom mirror for someone at home to solve.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 355, 'Find a sunny spot on the floor on a winter afternoon and write there like a cat in the warmth.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 356, 'Mix two clichés into one new phrase, like "a piece of cake in the dark," and write a line around it.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 357, 'Notice the shadows in your bedroom just before you turn off the light and describe their shapes.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 358, 'Mix a fairy and a plumber in one short scene where they fix a leaky faucet together.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 359, 'Imagine a bake sale for friendly monsters and write the labels for five of its goodies.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 360, 'Close your notebook with a silly sign off line, like a wave goodbye to the page.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 361, 'End your evening with a two line poem about the lamp beside you.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 362, 'Picture a winter afternoon at a frozen pond or icy sidewalk and describe its sounds, cracks and shine.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 363, 'Enjoy writing a scene that goes nowhere at all, two friends on a porch on a warm evening, just for the fun of it.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 364, 'Read out a list of made up words at dinner and let everyone guess what each one means.'),
  ('writing-just-for-fun', 365, 'Write a whole page in very tiny handwriting, as if for a mouse, and admire how small it looks.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 1, 'At midmorning, stop for a moment and ask yourself whether your energy feels full, half full or low.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 2, 'Look at your list and put the hardest task in the hour when you usually feel most awake.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 3, 'Stop a task while you still have a little energy left, instead of waiting until you feel worn out.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 4, 'Keep a little energy in reserve for the evening by leaving one small task on your list for another day.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 5, 'Tell your partner or roommate plainly when you are low on energy, so they know why you are quiet tonight.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 6, 'Write down the time today when you felt most awake and clear headed.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 7, 'Split a big chore like cleaning the kitchen into two sittings, one in the morning and one later on.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 8, 'Sit down for two minutes after you finish washing the dishes, before you start the next chore.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 9, 'Make an easy dinner on a long day, like eggs and toast or soup from the pantry, and call it enough.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 10, 'Share one chore with someone you live with, like one person washing while the other dries.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 11, 'Pick one word to describe your energy right after you wake up, such as foggy, slow, bright or restless.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 12, 'Leave a gap of at least ten minutes between two meetings or errands today.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 13, 'Stand up and stretch your arms overhead between one task and the next at your desk.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 14, 'Spend a quiet hour at home after a party or a big gathering, with soft lights and no plans.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 15, 'Ask a coworker kindly if a late afternoon meeting could move to a time when you have more energy.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 16, 'Notice when the afternoon dip shows up today and what you were doing just before it arrived.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 17, 'Choose one big thing for today and let the rest of your list stay small.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 18, 'Pour a glass of water at midafternoon and drink it slowly while you roll your shoulders.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 19, 'Allow yourself a slower morning after a late night, letting the first hour be calm and unhurried.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 20, 'Build a rest stop into a family outing, like a bench, a picnic blanket or a café break.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 21, 'Check your shoulders while you answer messages and see whether they have crept up toward your ears.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 22, 'Batch a few small tasks, like replying to texts, watering plants and sorting mail, into one short block.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 23, 'Close your eyes for one minute after a long stretch of reading or screen time.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 24, 'Leave one weekend slot open on purpose, with nothing planned for it at all.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 25, 'Spread holiday baking over several winter evenings instead of doing it all in one long day.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 26, 'Name one task today that left you feeling lighter once it was finished.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 27, 'Say a gentle no to one extra errand today: "Not today, but maybe later this week."'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 28, 'Perch on a chair to put on your shoes rather than balancing, and take an extra breath there before heading out.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 29, 'Give your Sunday a gentle shape: one small chore, one restful thing, and plenty of space between.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 30, 'Save outdoor chores for the cooler morning on hot summer days, and rest in the shade during the afternoon.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 31, 'Jot down one task that left you feeling drained, and leave it on the page without judging yourself.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 32, 'Put the tasks that need the most talking, like calls or meetings, on different days instead of stacking them together.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 33, 'Choose a slow walk around the block when you notice yourself pushing on through a heavy afternoon.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 34, 'Unpack only the essentials the night you get home from a trip, and let the rest wait until you have rested.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 35, 'Wrap up outdoor jobs earlier on shorter fall days, and let the early dark be a cue to slow down.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 36, 'Listen for the first yawn of the day and notice what time it comes and where you are.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 37, 'Pack tomorrow''s bag tonight so the morning asks a little less of you.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 38, 'Pause at the end of a paragraph, a page or an email, since a natural break point makes stopping easier.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 39, 'Let the dishes sit until morning on a night when you are truly tired.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 40, 'Offer a neighbor a spring trade: you water their plants one week and they water yours the next, so you each get a break.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 41, 'Describe your energy after a talk with a friend in a single word, like warmed, tired or buzzing.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 42, 'Lay out tomorrow''s clothes before bed so there is one fewer choice when you wake.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 43, 'Set the laundry basket down on the bed and sit beside it for a moment before you start folding.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 44, 'Change into comfortable clothes as soon as you get home, as a signal that the work part of the day is done.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 45, 'Break a long road trip into stages, with a stop every couple of hours to stretch and walk around.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 46, 'Look around the room you spend the most time in and ask whether it tends to perk you up or wear you down.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 47, 'Write tomorrow''s most important task on a sticky note and leave it where you will see it first.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 48, 'Rest your hands in your lap for three slow breaths after you hang up a phone call.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 49, 'Dim the lights an hour before bed and pick a calm activity for the rest of the evening.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 50, 'Sit down with your kids for a quiet story or puzzle in the middle of a busy afternoon together.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 51, 'Sit for a minute after lunch and notice how your body feels compared with before you ate.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 52, 'Group your errands by where they are so you make one loop instead of several trips.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 53, 'Look out a window at something far away for a minute when your eyes feel tired from close work.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 54, 'Lay a soft blanket over the couch before you leave in the morning, so it is waiting when you get home tired.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 55, 'Let a friend know you would love to meet, but for an hour rather than the whole afternoon.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 56, 'Keep a small note today with one word for your energy in the morning, at noon and in the evening.'),
  ('pacing-your-energy-through-the-day', 57, 'Leave the task that needs the most decisions for after a short break, not right after a long meeting.'),
